* Later rounds of competitive auctions (tables)

Phase 4 (NOTES.md #P6). The competitive counterpart of `later-rounds.bml`,
written out per auction where the calls depend on the suits: opener's answer
to a negative double of a two-level overcall, the continuations after
responder's raise or notrump over a one-level overcall, and the overcaller's
side after an advance. Every continuation ends with the partnership passing.

** Opener's answer to a negative double of a two-level overcall

The double shows the values to compete, usually with the unbid major(s).
Opener bids a four-card unbid major at the cheapest level with 12--15 and at
game with 16+ (hearts before spades), bids 2NT with 12--14 balanced and a
stopper, 3NT with 18--19, and otherwise makes the cheapest rebid of the
opening suit, which carries no requirement of its own (the double is
forcing). Responder then passes.

1C-(2D)-D-(P)-
4H = {prio:5} 16+ hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
2H = {prio:5} 12--15 hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
4S = {prio:4} 16+ hcp, 4+!s
  #PASTE after-chain
2S = {prio:4} 12--15 hcp, 4+!s
  #PASTE after-chain
2N = {prio:2} 12--14 hcp, bal, stopper
  #PASTE after-chain
3N = {prio:2} 18--19 hcp, bal, stopper
  #PASTE after-chain
3C = {prio:-1} any hand
  #PASTE after-chain

